cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Code Futures"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
abstract: >-
  Given a repository, say what state its engineering practice is in. Code
  Futures reports on code structure — where complexity and churn concentrate,
  which files keep changing together, where a module boundary is leaking — and
  on the practice around it: linting, testing, review gates, dependency
  hygiene, and the open-source baseline. It produces a report per repository
  and a machine-readable snapshot, and knows nothing about courses, teams, or
  people. The name follows Kent Beck's framing of features, which are what
  software does now, against futures, which are what remains possible later.
authors:
  - given-names: Daniel
    family-names: Shown
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-5716-8835"
    affiliation: Saint Louis University
repository-code: "https://github.com/oss-slu/code-futures"
url: "https://github.com/oss-slu/code-futures"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-30"
keywords:
  - static analysis
  - software quality
  - technical debt
  - change coupling
  - computing education
  - open source program office
references:
  - type: book
    title: "Tidy First? A Personal Exercise in Empirical Software Design"
    authors:
      - given-names: Kent
        family-names: Beck
    publisher:
      name: O'Reilly Media
    year: 2023
    isbn: "9781098151249"
    notes: >-
      Source of the coupling and cohesion definitions the structural analysis
      measures, of the cost argument behind the blast-radius finding, and of
      the question the tidy-first finding answers.
  # `video` rather than `audiovisual`. The CFF schema defines neither --
  # `type` carries one description, "The type of the work", and 47 bare enum
  # values with no per-value definitions and no selection guidance. Both
  # would validate. `video` is chosen because the vocabulary also contains
  # `film-broadcast`, `sound-recording`, `multimedia` and `slides`: in a list
  # that fine-grained the specific value is the intended one, or `video`
  # would never be right for anything.
  - type: video
    title: "Features Versus Futures"
    authors:
      - given-names: Kent
        family-names: Beck
    year: 2026
    url: "https://videos.itrevolution.com/watch/1183714411/"
    notes: >-
      Source of the features-versus-futures framing the tool is named for.
      The underlying argument, that structure creates options rather than
      value today, is developed in Tidy First?.
  - type: book
    title: "Your Code as a Crime Scene"
    authors:
      - given-names: Adam
        family-names: Tornhill
    publisher:
      name: Pragmatic Bookshelf
    year: 2015
    isbn: "9781680500387"
    notes: >-
      Source of the hotspot and change-coupling techniques computed from git
      history, and of the indentation-based complexity proxy.
